most prevalent manifestation of lead poisoning in children
is central neurotoxicity [11]. Other symptoms associated
with childhood lead toxicity include anemia, peripheral
motor neuropathy, and gastrointestinal issues such as
anorexia, vomiting, and abdominal pain, as well as growth
delays [12].

